{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27364,"name":"Steven Hert","username":"Steven_Hert","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/steven_hert/{size}/12057_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:01:14.810Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’ve started building \u003cstrong\u003eckbup\u003c/strong\u003e, a small open-source installer and version manager for CKB’s command-line tools, in the spirit of \u003ccode\u003erustup\u003c/code\u003e. It’s free and I’m not asking for anything; I’m sharing it early to get feedback from people who actually set up CKB machines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27364-why-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27364-why-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhy\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGetting the CKB tools onto a machine still means a different route for each one:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethere’s no package-manager install for \u003ccode\u003eckb-cli\u003c/code\u003e, only “manually downloading a \u003ccode\u003e.zip\u003c/code\u003e/\u003ccode\u003e.tar.gz\u003c/code\u003e from the Releases page” (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-cli/issues/685\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eckb-cli#685\u003c/a\u003e);\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003esome tools ship no arm64 builds, so ARM users build from source, which “works but takes 20-30 min” (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-light-client/issues/272\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eckb-light-client#272\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/fiber/issues/1186\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003efiber#1186\u003c/a\u003e);\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ecargo install ckb-cli\u003c/code\u003e fails on Windows (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-cli/issues/660\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eckb-cli#660\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen someone asked in the DevRel AMA about installing tools as one bundle, the answer was that “Bundling them in a separate project should be relatively straightforward” (\u003ca href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/t/10794/5\"\u003et/10794/5\u003c/a\u003e). ckbup is my attempt at that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27364-what-works-today-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27364-what-works-today-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat works today\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe first step is merged: \u003ccode\u003eckbup install\u003c/code\u003e for \u003cstrong\u003eckb-debugger\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eckb-cli\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIt picks the right official release file for your OS and CPU.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIt checks every download’s SHA-256 against the digest GitHub publishes for the release asset, and against the project’s own checksum file where there is one. A mismatch deletes the download and installs nothing.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIt installs into \u003ccode\u003e~/.ckbup\u003c/code\u003e and tells you how to add it to your PATH.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo try it (needs Rust):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003ecargo install --git https://github.com/steven3002/ckbup\nckbup install ckb-debugger\nckbup install ckb-cli\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepo: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/steven3002/ckbup\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGitHub - steven3002/ckbup: Installer and version manager for CKB tools: ckb, ckb-cli, ckb-debugger, fnn and more. · GitHub\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27364-what-i-found-about-the-releases-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27364-what-i-found-about-the-releases-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhat I found about the releases\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery tool publishes differently:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eTool\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eLatest\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003earm64 builds\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eWindows\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eChecksums\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eckb\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev0.210.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLinux, macOS\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ex86_64\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003esignature files\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eckb-cli\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev2.0.0\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLinux, macOS\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ex86_64\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003esignature files\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eckb-debugger\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev1.1.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eLinux, macOS\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ex86_64\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003echecksum file\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003efnn\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev0.9.1\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eportable builds only\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ex86_64\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003enone\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eckb-light-client\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev0.5.4\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003enone in the stable release\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ex86_64\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003enone\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003emoleculec\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ev0.9.2\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno release binaries (\u003ca href=\"http://crates.io\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ecrates.io\u003c/a\u003e only)\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003enone\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003enone\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo tool ships Windows arm64 builds yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27364-next-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27364-next-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eNext\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe other four tools (\u003ccode\u003eckb\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eckb-light-client\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003emoleculec\u003c/code\u003e);\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003elist\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003euse\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eupdate\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eremove\u003c/code\u003e;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ea source-build fallback where no arm64 binary exists;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCI across Linux, macOS and Windows, then a v0.1.0 release.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27364-feedback-welcome-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27364-feedback-welcome-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFeedback welcome\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhich tools and platforms matter most to you?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you run CKB on ARM boards or in CI, what breaks today?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAnything wrong in the table above? I’d like it to be accurate.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-11T19:01:14.810Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":95.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":11188,"topic_slug":"ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome","display_username":"Steven Hert","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://crates.io","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"crates.io: Rust Package Registry","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-cli/issues/685","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Improve installation/distribution: crates.io, Homebrew tap, Scoop bucket, install script · Issue #685 · nervosnetwork/ckb-cli · GitHub","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-light-client/issues/272","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"arm64 binaries not included in v0.5.4 release (PR #265 merged after tag) · Issue #272 · nervosnetwork/ckb-light-client · GitHub","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/fiber/issues/1186","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"feat: add aarch64-linux prebuilt binary to release workflow · Issue #1186 · nervosnetwork/fiber · GitHub","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb-cli/issues/660","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"error: failed to run custom build command for 'ckb-vm v0.22.1' · Issue #660 · nervosnetwork/ckb-cli · GitHub","clicks":0},{"url":"https://talk.nervos.org/t/ckba-dev-rel-ama/10794/5","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"CKBA Dev Rel AMA","clicks":0},{"url":"https://github.com/steven3002/ckbup","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub - steven3002/ckbup: Installer and version manager for CKB tools: ckb, ckb-cli, ckb-debugger, fnn and more. · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":3}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4521,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome/11188/1","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":3}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":3,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false,"can_translate":false},{"id":27412,"name":"Steven Hert","username":"Steven_Hert","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/steven_hert/{size}/12057_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-14T08:14:57.786Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUpdate: ckbup now installs five tools.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe second step is merged. \u003ccode\u003eckbup install\u003c/code\u003e now covers \u003cstrong\u003eckb\u003c/strong\u003e, \u003cstrong\u003efnn\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eckb-light-client\u003c/strong\u003e as well as ckb-debugger and ckb-cli.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003ecargo install --git https://github.com/steven3002/ckbup\nckbup install ckb\nckbup install fnn\nckbup install ckb-light-client\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat changed:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe right build for your machine.\u003c/strong\u003e Each project names its release files differently, and ckbup reads each scheme. For fnn and ckb-light-client it prefers the \u003cstrong\u003eportable\u003c/strong\u003e builds: their standard Linux builds need glibc 2.39 and 2.38, while the portable ones run on glibc 2.34. \u003ccode\u003e--portable\u003c/code\u003e asks for the portable build where a project publishes one. ckb’s release notes recommend it if you see “illegal instruction” errors. CentOS builds are skipped, since upstream plans to stop shipping them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhole release packages.\u003c/strong\u003e Config folders and docs stay next to the binary, and companion tools such as \u003ccode\u003efnn-cli\u003c/code\u003e go on your PATH too. The copy of \u003ccode\u003eckb-cli\u003c/code\u003e bundled inside the ckb release is left off PATH, because ckbup manages \u003ccode\u003eckb-cli\u003c/code\u003e as its own tool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChecksums, or a clear stop.\u003c/strong\u003e Every download is checked against the SHA-256 that GitHub publishes for the release file. Releases published before mid-2025 usually have no checksum at all, so ckbup refuses them unless you pass \u003ccode\u003e--allow-unverified\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003e$ ckbup install ckb-light-client@v0.4.1\nerror: GitHub lists no SHA-256 for ckb-light-client_v0.4.1-x86_64-windows.tar.gz, and ckb-light-client\npublishes no checksum file for v0.4.1; older releases often have none. Re-run with --allow-unverified\nto install it without verification\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt also picked up Fiber’s \u003cstrong\u003efnn v0.10.1\u003c/strong\u003e, released this week, as soon as it appeared.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Windows, ckb-light-client needs the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime; the README says so.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNext:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003elist\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003euse\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eremove\u003c/code\u003e, so you can see what’s installed and switch between versions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you run fnn or the light client on an older Linux, I’d like to hear whether the portable builds work for you.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-14T08:14:57.786Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":22,"readers_count":21,"score":24.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":11188,"topic_slug":"ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome","display_username":"Steven Hert","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4521,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome/11188/2","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":27565,"name":"Steven Hert","username":"Steven_Hert","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/steven_hert/{size}/12057_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-18T21:11:57.313Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUpdate: ckbup can now list, switch and remove versions.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe third step is merged. You can see what’s installed, switch between versions and remove the ones you don’t need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003ecargo install --git https://github.com/steven3002/ckbup\nckbup list                  # every tool, its installed versions and the active one\nckbup list --available      # the newest stable releases, with notes for your machine\nckbup use fnn@v0.9.1        # switch to another installed version\nckbup remove fnn@v0.10.1    # remove one you no longer need\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eckbup list\u003c/code\u003e on my machine:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eckb               v0.210.0 (active)\nckb-cli           v2.0.0 (active)\nckb-debugger      v1.1.1 (active)\nfnn               v0.10.1 (active)\nckb-light-client  v0.5.4 (active)\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat changed:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003elist\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e shows all five tools, with installed versions newest first and the active one marked. \u003ccode\u003eckbup list fnn\u003c/code\u003e also shows where each version lives.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003elist --available\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e shows the newest 10 stable releases of each tool, and whether your machine has a build and a checksum for each. Releases without a checksum still need \u003ccode\u003e--allow-unverified\u003c/code\u003e. It uses one GitHub request per tool.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003euse\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e switches versions offline. If the version isn’t installed, it prints the install command instead of downloading anything. fnn’s \u003ccode\u003efnn-cli\u003c/code\u003e switches along with \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ccode\u003eremove\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e won’t delete the version you’re using while other versions are installed; switch with \u003ccode\u003euse\u003c/code\u003e first. Removing a tool’s last version also takes it off your PATH.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSwitching works while a tool is running.\u003c/strong\u003e Windows won’t let a running program be overwritten, so ckbup moves the old files aside instead, and a running program doesn’t block a switch.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eInstalling a second version\u003c/strong\u003e leaves the current one active, and ckbup tells you how to switch.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTested on Windows and on Ubuntu 26.04.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNext:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003eupdate\u003c/code\u003e, downloads that resume after a dropped connection, and an optional cache so that switching back to an older version needs no new download.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI haven’t been able to test on macOS yet. If you’re on a Mac, I’d like to hear whether \u003ccode\u003euse\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eremove\u003c/code\u003e work for you.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":3,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-18T21:11:57.313Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":2,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":17.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":11188,"topic_slug":"ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome","display_username":"Steven Hert","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":4521,"username":"Steven_Hert","name":"Steven Hert","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/steven_hert/{size}/12057_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4521,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/ckbup-one-installer-for-ckb-command-line-tools-early-progress-feedback-welcome/11188/3","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"